[b][size=5]Bulk Load[/size][/b]

Pawns use their inventory to carry more. Fewer walks, no new items, just Harmony required.

[b][size=4]Unloading pack animals in one pass[/size][/b]
No more leading every muffalo through the stockpile one stack at a time. Walk up once, grab the whole load, shelve it.

Vanilla:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/BPqYND6skkXPMaWwae/giphy.gif[/img]

Bulk Load:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/mscDCIHhiYisg42GeH/giphy.gif[/img]

[b][size=4]Bulk-loading transporters[/size][/b]
Pods, shuttles and pit gates get loaded in full hands instead of single-stack trips.

Vanilla:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/Nrx9DsFqc55TNyCKKh/giphy.gif[/img]

Bulk Load:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/ClHxAEhjaheBHDLl8u/giphy.gif[/img]

[b][size=4]Crafting in one trip[/size][/b]
Bills gather every ingredient for a recipe at once instead of one pawn per ingredient type.

Vanilla:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/6UezHboOSlBQ0JHZzs/giphy.gif[/img]

Bulk Load:
[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/LWxQMrSjAfW9M5246J/giphy.gif[/img]

[b][size=4]Also included[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Bulk-loading Anomaly portals
[*]Unload leftover goods: if you use Combat Extended and returning caravan members hold onto goods instead of shelving them, this option in Mod Settings might help (it may also be worth checking whether they have a CE loadout assigned)
[/list]

[b][size=4]Compatibility[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Requires Harmony, nothing else
[*]Drives vanilla jobs and storage, so it plays nice with stack mods and storage mods
[*]Respects encumbrance, storage settings and food/drug keeps
[/list]

Works best with increased carry capacity. The bigger the pockets, the fewer the trips.
